4.10.1 Fuzzy time doesn't appear in mode-line
---------------------------------------------

Check that ‘global-mode-string’ is included in your mode-line format:

     ;; Evaluate this to check:
     global-mode-string

     ;; Should include: (:eval fuzzy-clock-string)

   If it's missing, your mode-line configuration might be overriding the
default.


File: fuzzy-clock.info,  Node: Mode-line shows "*invalid*",  Next: Fuzzy time doesn't update,  Prev: Fuzzy time doesn't appear in mode-line,  Up: Troubleshooting

4.10.2 Mode-line shows "*invalid*"
----------------------------------

This happens if ‘fuzzy-clock-string’ isn't marked as a risky variable.

   Fuzzy-clock sets this automatically, but some configurations might
block it.

   Check:

     (get 'fuzzy-clock-string 'risky-local-variable)
     ;; Should return: t

   If it returns ‘nil’, manually set it:

     (put 'fuzzy-clock-string 'risky-local-variable t)


File: fuzzy-clock.info,  Node: Fuzzy time doesn't update,  Next: Wrong season displayed (Southern Hemisphere),  Prev: Mode-line shows "*invalid*",  Up: Troubleshooting

4.10.3 Fuzzy time doesn't update
--------------------------------

Check that the timer is running:

     fuzzy-clock-timer
     ;; Should return a timer object like: [t 0 60 60 fuzzy-clock-update nil nil]

   If it's ‘nil’, the timer isn't running.  Try:

     (fuzzy-clock-mode 0)
     (fuzzy-clock-mode 1)


File: fuzzy-clock.info,  Node: Wrong season displayed (Southern Hemisphere),  Prev: Fuzzy time doesn't update,  Up: Troubleshooting

4.10.4 Wrong season displayed (Southern Hemisphere)
---------------------------------------------------

The season definitions are Northern Hemisphere by default.

   Current workaround: The season feature isn't customizable yet.

   Future enhancement: Add customization for hemisphere.


